    "summary": "Docker containers and virtual machines both isolate workloads but differ fundamentally: containers share the host OS kernel for lightweight, fast deployments, while VMs emulate full hardware for stronger isolation. Choosing between them depends on your security requirements, performance needs, and workload type.",
